		<published>2025-02-28T08:18:20</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4919&amp;p=36001#p36001</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4919&amp;p=36001#p36001"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: V5 MD9600 &quot;TG 9 - Out Of Band&quot;]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4919&amp;p=36001#p36001"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi,<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>For the ones who are experiencing codeplug corruption, please try these firmwares and <strong class="text-strong">REPORT</strong> if it works (or not):<br><a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/PB0DP8TTJC#Hh0aZNxb9euj" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/PB0DP8TTJC#Hh0aZNxb9euj</a><br><br>In case that solves the problem, I will release a new beta for the MD-9600 (only).<br><br><strong class="text-strong">EDIT</strong>: I forgot to mention, once the codeplug is corrupted, it's corrupted. You need to re-flash it after flashing the firmware.</div></blockquote>I updated the firmware that you posted above. I did it how you suggested above and loaded the refreshed code plug that you sent back to me and so far so good.<br><br>My V5 9600 works every time after a power cycle with no errors. Can select any zone, channel and then power cycle the radio and it powers back up with no errors. I'll continue to monitor it over the coming days.<br><br>May I ask, how can I in the future determine if my code plug is corrupted to assist with my own troubleshooting?<br><br>Many thanks for your assistance Daniel.<br><br>Cheers<br><br>VK4GAN</div></blockquote>Great.<br>Well, if you notice some weird value (like crazy ColorCodem, Power, FM channel becoming DMR by their own, CTCSS/DCS self enabling value, unwanted boot image/melody changes and stuff like that), you can suspect codeplug corruption.<br>On the CPS side, after reading the codeplug from the transceiver, and noticing weird values in channels, or unmanageable zones, you can suspect some corruption.<br>It's always good to store codeplug evolutions stages, as you can go back before the corruption. Another one is to export and store the CSV files generated by the CPS, as it's fast and easy to rebuild a codeplug from scratch.<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>Cheers Daniel <br><br>Understood. Will be more diligent with all this moving forward.<br><br>Again appreciate your time and patience.<br><br>Cheers and 73,<br><br>VK4GAN<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6488">VK4GAN</a> — Fri Feb 28, 2025 8:18 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
