		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4919&amp;p=35999#p35999"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Can it be some other issue that corrupts the stored codeplug ?<br>Some memory corruption ?</div></blockquote>Make sure you use the latest CPS and the latest Firmware. Do NOT mix older FW or older CPS with their newer versions. Keep your radios and the CPS on the same version. If you upgrade, read the codeplug into the new CPS version and then re-write the Codeplug back into the radio after the FW is upgraded. <br><br>One more possiblity is, that a radio has a weak memory battery. My oldest 9600, a v2, starts to act up a bit if i haven't used it for  week or longer. Usally it goes into the "Settings updated" screen, but one never know.<br><br>just my 2 cents on this...</div></blockquote>That's a great tip and i should have also followed that as I would have done with my 878uvii as they advise you to do after a firmware update as the CPS is supposed to match the firmware version and reading from the radio before writing to it.<br><br>Cheers,<br><br>VK4GAN<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6488">VK4GAN</a> — Fri Feb 28, 2025 7:32 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
